    "title": "Agent set a git config that executes code or captures credentials",
    "desc": "An agent account set a git config key that runs code or steals credentials, or wrote a git hook directly. core.hooksPath / core.fsmonitor / core.sshCommand / core.pager run a command on an ordinary git operation; credential.helper captures the credentials of whoever next uses the checkout; include.path / filter.*.clean / alias with a `!` shell escape are the same. A coding agent runs git all day and never sets these. The payload fires on *the human's* machine or his next pull - persistence that leaves the agent's account entirely. SigmaHQ has no git-config-persistence rule; this is useful on any host, not just for agents.",
    "analytic": {
